From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tanjilbhuiyan <tanjilbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:42:43 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 53/56] Input: melfas_mip4 - take the event format from the
 device tree if unreported

Samsung's MSS100 firmware (Galaxy A50) answers the MIP4 information
registers but reports an event size of 0 and no event format, while it
sends format 8 events of 12 bytes; Samsung's own driver takes both from
its device tree. Add optional melfas,event-format and melfas,event-size
properties that are used only when the controller reports no event size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I27854c14fae05d9d7440cb4f498299d93fe084de
---
 .../input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.txt         |  5 ++++
 drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c       | 29 ++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.txt b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.txt
index b2ab5498e..d6d4a061d 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.txt
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.txt
@@ -7,6 +7,11 @@ Required properties:
 
 Optional properties:
 - ce-gpios: GPIO connected to the CE (chip enable) pin of the chip
+- melfas,event-format: MIP4 event packet format, used only when the controller
+  firmware does not report one (it reports an event size of 0), as with Samsung
+  MSS100 firmware
+- melfas,event-size: size in bytes of one event in that format (required with
+  melfas,event-format)
 
 Example:
 	i2c@00000000 {
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c
index b9502d1ca..69fa0b364 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/melfas_mip4.c
@@ -355,12 +355,33 @@ static int mip4_query_device(struct mip4_ts *ts)
 		dev_dbg(&ts->client->dev, "event_format: %d, event_size: %d\n",
 			ts->event_format, ts->event_size);
 
-		if (ts->event_format == 2 ||
-		    (ts->event_format > 3 && ts->event_format != 8))
-			dev_warn(&ts->client->dev,
-				 "Unknown event format %d\n", ts->event_format);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Some firmware (Samsung MSS100) does not report its event format and
+	 * size; the device tree may then provide them.
+	 */
+	if (!ts->event_size) {
+		u32 format, size;
+
+		if (!device_property_read_u32(&ts->client->dev,
+					      "melfas,event-format", &format) &&
+		    !device_property_read_u32(&ts->client->dev,
+					      "melfas,event-size", &size) &&
+		    size > 0 && size <= MIP4_BUF_SIZE) {
+			ts->event_format = format;
+			ts->event_size = size;
+			dev_dbg(&ts->client->dev,
+				"event format %u, size %u from device tree\n",
+				format, size);
+		}
+	}
+
+	if (ts->event_format == 2 ||
+	    (ts->event_format > 3 && ts->event_format != 8))
+		dev_warn(&ts->client->dev,
+			 "Unknown event format %d\n", ts->event_format);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
